n### Q: What do you need from me to activate my card?\nA: Typically the last four digits of the card, your full date of birth including the year, and your postal code.\n\n### Q: Why do you need my date of birth and postal code?\nA: It’s a security step to make sure I’m speaking with the right cardholder and to protect your account.\n\n### Q: Do I need to key in digits on my phone?\nA: No — you can just say the information out loud naturally. No keypad entries needed.\n\n### Q: I said my date of birth but I didn’t include the year — is that okay?\nA: I’ll just need the year as well to complete verification. What year were you born?\n\n### Q: How should I say my postal code?\nA: You can say it normally, or letter-by-letter if that’s easier — for example, “M five H one J eight.”\n\n### Q: My activation didn’t work — what can we do?\nA: We can try again and confirm the details I captured. If it still doesn’t go through, I’ll connect you with a representative to resolve it.\n\n### Q: How long does activation take?\nA: Usually just a moment once verification passes.\n\n### Q: Is my card ready to use immediately after activation?\nA: Yes — once I confirm it’s activated, it’s ready to use.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Rewards - Earning\n\n### Q: How do Walmart Reward Dollars work?\nA: You earn Walmart Reward Dollars on eligible purchases, and you can redeem them toward eligible purchases once they’re available.\n\n### Q: What are the earn rates?\nA: You earn 3% in Walmart Reward Dollars on eligible purchases at Walmart stores in Canada or on Walmart.ca, and 1% on eligible purchases everywhere else.\n\n### Q: Do rewards apply to everything I buy?\nA: Rewards apply to eligible purchases. The program terms list categories or transactions that may be excluded.\n\n### Q: Do I earn Reward Dollars on taxes, fees, or shipping?\nA: Eligibility can depend on how the program terms define “eligible purchases.” I can send you the official program terms if you want the exact wording.\n\n### Q: Do rewards reverse if I return something?\nA: Yes — if a purchase is refunded, the Reward Dollars associated with it typically reverse once the return posts.\n\n### Q: Is there a limit to how many Reward Dollars I can earn?\nA: In the program terms used for this demo, there’s no limit as long as your account is in good standing.\n\n### Q: Do Reward Dollars expire?\nA: In the program terms used for this demo, Reward Dollars do not expire as long as your account is in good standing.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Rewards - Posting & Timing\n\n### Q: When do Reward Dollars show up?\nA: Typically once the purchase posts — usually the next business day. If it’s not a banking day, it can take a short delay.\n\n### Q: Why don’t I see my Reward Dollars yet?\nA: The purchase may still be pending, or it may be an excluded category. If you tell me roughly when and where you bought it, I can help narrow it down.\n\n### Q: Do pending transactions earn rewards right away?\nA: Rewards typically appear after the purchase posts, not while it’s pending.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Rewards - Redemption Basics\n\n### Q: How do I redeem Walmart Reward Dollars?\nA: You redeem them toward eligible purchases at checkout where redemption is supported, following the minimum and restriction rules.\n\n### Q: What’s the minimum amount I can redeem?\nA: The minimum redemption is $5 in Walmart Reward Dollars.\n\n### Q: Do I have to redeem in increments?\nA: Yes — after the $5 minimum, redemption is in $5 increments.\n\n### Q: Can I redeem online at Walmart.ca?\nA: Yes, redemption is available online where supported — with the same minimum/increment rules and restrictions.\n\n### Q: Can I redeem in store?\nA: Yes, where supported. If you tell me what you’re trying to buy, I can confirm the common restriction categories.\n\n### Q: Can I redeem Reward Dollars for cash?\nA: No — Reward Dollars can’t be redeemed for cash.\n\n### Q: Why is my redemption not working?\nA: Common reasons are being under the $5 minimum, trying to redeem for a restricted category, or using a payment method that doesn’t support redemption.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Rewards - Redemption Restrictions\n\n### Q: Are there redemption restrictions?\nA: Yes — Reward Dollars can’t be redeemed for cash and can’t be redeemed for certain restricted categories.\n\n### Q: Can I redeem Reward Dollars for alcohol?\nA: No — alcohol is a restricted category for redemption.\n\n### Q: Can I redeem Reward Dollars for tobacco?\nA: No — tobacco is restricted.\n\n### Q: Can I redeem Reward Dollars for lottery tickets?\nA: No — lottery is restricted.\n\n### Q: Can I redeem Reward Dollars for prescription medication?\nA: No — prescription medication is restricted.\n\n### Q: Can I redeem Reward Dollars for gift cards?\nA: That depends on the specific program restriction list. I can send you the official program terms for the exact rule.\n\n### Q: Can I redeem Reward Dollars for cash back or statement credit?\nA: Reward Dollars are intended to be redeemed toward eligible purchases rather than cash. The program terms describe the supported redemption methods.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Mobile Wallet (Apple Pay / Google Pay)\n\n### Q: Can I add my card to Apple Pay or Google Pay?\nA: Mobile wallet support depends on the program setup. I can confirm what’s supported from the official FAQs.\n\n### Q: Can I redeem Reward Dollars when paying with Apple Pay or Google Pay?\nA: At the moment, Reward Dollars can’t be redeemed in-store or online through mobile wallet.\n\n### Q: Can I still earn Reward Dollars if I pay with a mobile wallet?\nA: Earning is based on eligible purchases. Redemption through mobile wallet is the part that’s currently restricted.\n\n### Q: Why can’t I redeem Reward Dollars through mobile wallet?\nA: It’s a current program limitation. If you want, I can explain the supported way to redeem that works today.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Online Account Access & Self-Serve\n\n### Q: How do I manage my account online?\nA: You can sign in at walmartrewardsmc.ca to view your balance, statements, and transactions.\n\n### Q: Where can I see my balance and transactions?\nA: In the online account portal and on your statements.\n\n### Q: How do I get statements?\nA: Statements are available in your online account portal.\n\n### Q: How do I update my address, phone number, or email?\nA: You can update many details through the portal. If anything requires servicing, I can connect you to customer service.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Card Not Received / Lost / Stolen / Fraud\n\n### Q: I didn’t receive my card — what should I do?\nA: We’ll treat that as a “card not received” case and arrange a replacement. I can connect you to a representative.\n\n### Q: My card is lost or stolen — what should I do?\nA: Report it right away so the card can be blocked and replaced. I can transfer you now.\n\n### Q: I see a charge I don’t recognize — what do I do?\nA: Disputes and fraud issues are handled by the servicing team so they can secure the account. I can connect you immediately.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Payments & Statements (General)\n\n### Q: How do I make a payment?\nA: You can make payments through the account portal or supported banking/payment options. If you tell me what method you prefer, I can guide you or connect you.\n\n### Q: When is my payment due?\nA: Your due date is shown on your statement and in your online account. If you’d like, I can connect you to confirm the exact date.\n\n### Q: What is the minimum payment?\nA: It depends on your statement balance and agreement terms. Your statement will show the exact minimum payment due.\n\n### Q: How long does it take for a payment to post?\nA: Posting time varies by payment method and banking day. If you tell me how you paid, I can give the typical range or connect you.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Customer Service & Escalation\n\n### Q: What’s the customer service number?\nA: For account questions, customer service is 1-888-331-6133.\n\n### Q: Can I speak to a representative?\nA: Absolutely — I can transfer you now.\n\n### Q: When do you transfer to a human?\nA: If you request it, if verification fails after retries, or if you need licensed insurance advice or eligibility decisions.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Balance Protection Plan (BPP) - Overview\n\n### Q: What is Balance Protection Plan (BPP)?\nA: It’s optional balance protection insurance underwritten by Canada Life and offered through Fairstone. Depending on the covered event, it may make monthly payments toward your card balance.\n\n### Q: Is BPP required?\nA: No — not at all. Your card works the same either way. It’s optional.\n\n### Q: What does BPP cover?\nA: Depending on the covered event — like disability or involuntary job loss — it may make monthly payments toward your balance, and for certain covered events it may pay the balance up to a limit. The certificate has the full details.\n\n### Q: Does BPP pay off my whole balance?\nA: For certain covered events it may pay the balance up to a limit. The certificate explains benefit limits and how payments work.\n\n### Q: Can you tell me if I should buy it?\nA: I can explain what the certificate says, but I can’t advise what you personally should buy. If you’d like, I can send the certificate or connect you to a licensed advisor.\n\n---\n\n## 12. BPP - Cost, Premium, Examples\n\n### Q: How much does BPP cost?\nA: The premium is calculated from your monthly statement balance: $1.09 per $100, plus applicable taxes.\n\n### Q: Can you give me an example premium?\nA: Sure — if your statement balance were $500, the premium would be about $5.45 plus tax.\n\n### Q: Does the premium change?\nA: It can, because it’s calculated from your statement balance each month.\n\n### Q: Is there a premium if my balance is very low?\nA: If your statement balance is under $10, there may be no premium that month — the certificate explains the details.\n\n---\n\n## 13. BPP - Cancellation & Free Look\n\n### Q: Can I cancel BPP?\nA: Yes — you can cancel. The certificate includes cancellation steps.\n\n### Q: Is there a free look period?\nA: Yes — you may cancel within 30 days from the date coverage begins and receive a full refund of any premium paid.\n\n### Q: If I cancel, does it affect my card?\nA: No — it’s optional coverage. Canceling doesn’t affect your card’s ability to work.\n\n---\n\n## 14. BPP - Eligibility / Exclusions (Transfer-safe)\n\n### Q: Am I eligible for BPP?\nA: Eligibility is defined in the certificate. I can send the official certificate so you can review the exact requirements.\n\n### Q: I’m self-employed / contract / seasonal — would it cover me?\nA: Eligibility and exclusions depend on the certificate terms and your situation. I can send the official certificate, or connect you with a licensed insurance advisor — which do you prefer?\n\n### Q: What’s excluded?\nA: Exclusions depend on the certificate wording. I can send the official certificate so you can review the exact list.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Accident Insurance (Only If Asked)\n\n### Q: What is Accident Insurance for cardholders?\nA: It’s group accident insurance underwritten by Manulife and offered for Walmart Rewards Mastercard cardholders. I can summarize the official page and send the link.\n\n### Q: Can I enroll in Accident Insurance?\nA: If you’d like to enroll or get a quote, I can connect you to Manulife’s licensed advisors.\n\n---\n\n## 16. Voice Recovery & Security (Demo Realism)\n\n### Q: Can you repeat that?\nA: Of course. I can repeat it back, or we can try again — whichever you prefer.\n\n### Q: Why do you only repeat the last four digits?\nA: For security, I only repeat partial details. It helps verify without exposing sensitive information.\n\n### Q: I don’t feel comfortable saying that out loud — what are my options?\nA: That’s completely understandable. I can connect you to a representative for an alternate verification method.\n\n### Q: Will you text or email me information?\nA: I can — but only if you ask me to. Just tell me whether you prefer text or email, and I’ll send the official materials to the contact on file unless you provide a different destination.\n`;","hasError":false,"transpiled":"context.knowledge = `\n## Table of Contents\n\n1. [Activation & Verification (Speech-Only)](#1-activation--verification-speech-only)\n2. [Rewards - Earning](#2-rewards---earning)\n3. [Rewards - Posting & Timing](#3-rewards---posting--timing)\n4. [Rewards - Redemption Basics](#4-rewards---redemption-basics)\n5. [Rewards - Redemption Restrictions](#5-rewards---redemption-restrictions)\n6. [Mobile Wallet (Apple Pay / Google Pay)](#6-mobile-wallet-apple-pay--google-pay)\n7. [Online Account Access & Self-Serve](#7-online-account-access--self-serve)\n8. [Card Not Received / Lost / Stolen / Fraud](#8-card-not-received--lost--stolen--fraud)\n9. [Payments & Statements (General)](#9-payments--statements-general)\n10. [Customer Service & Escalation](#10-customer-service--escalation)\n11. [Balance Protection Plan (BPP) - Overview](#11-balance-protection-plan-bpp---overview)\n12. [BPP - Cost, Premium, Examples](#12-bpp---cost-premium-examples)\n13. [BPP - Cancellation & Free Look](#13-bpp---cancellation--free-look)\n14. [BPP - Eligibility / Exclusions (Transfer-safe)](#14-bpp---eligibility--exclusions-transfer-safe)\n15. [Accident Insurance (Only If Asked)](#15-accident-insurance-only-if-asked)\n16. [Voice Recovery & Security (Demo Realism)](#16-voice-recovery--security-demo-realism)\n\n---\n\n## 1. Activation & Verification (Speech-Only)\n\n### Q: How do I activate my Walmart Rewards Mastercard?\nA: You can activate it by phone. Since you’re already on the line, I can activate it for you right now after a quick verification.\n\n### Q: Can you activate my card for me on this call?\nA: Yes — I can do it now. I’ll just confirm a couple details to protect your account.\n\n### Q: What do you need from me to activate my card?\nA: Typically the last four digits of the card, your full date of birth including the year, and your postal code.\n\n### Q: Why do you need